# Integration Rules

## Linq
- Server-only SDK usage via `libs/linq/`
- Webhooks are the primary inbound path for the agent
- Conversational replies only — see `product.mdc`

## Terac
- Draft opportunities by default
- Launch only after explicit user/operator confirmation
- App runtime uses REST (`libs/terac/`), not Cursor MCP

## Dynamic
- Provider/widget in `components/dynamic/`
- Payment coordination logic in `libs/dynamic/` + `db/payments/`
- Never expose `DYNAMIC_API_KEY` to the client

## Cross-cutting
- Persist external IDs for chat, opportunity, submission, and payment
- Mirror important state changes back to the Linq thread
